35,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... I found that we're losing nearly an hour every day just copying records that already exist. Also, there were eleven misrouted deliveries because different units have different addresses for the same firm. It's... it's a lot of wasted effort.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, that's exactly what I feared! It's just more wasted effort. And guess what? My findings are even worse. Our coordination group is a ghost town, yet two poor souls are still doing everything by hand.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, ""ghost town"" is a bit dramatic, but the reality is just as bleak. I found that half our customer plants have dead zones for entire afternoons, and getting device approval takes six weeks. We're planning in a vacuum.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The financial situation is precarious. The capital budget is frozen, meaning we can only rely on the recurring software allowance. Furthermore, per-head licensing costs will increase as we scale, unlike fixed-fee work which remains stable.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, that's a big deal! But look, my findings show a pattern: big projects that require everyone to enter data daily just die out. Only the small, specialized tools for specific trades actually survive. We need to be careful!","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Kenji, that's... that's really important. If big projects fail because they're too demanding, then maybe we should focus on something that fixes those daily wastes I found, without adding more work for everyone.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, you've hit the nail on the head! We can't just throw another ""big project"" at people who are already drowning. My data shows we have zero extra hands to manage it. Who's going to do the work?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, exactly. We have no staff, no budget for new licenses, and we can't even get a signal at the plants. Any proposal promising a ""grand transformation"" is just a fantasy if the groundwork is this broken.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, I agree. Given the frozen capital budget and the risk of escalating per-head license costs, any proposal requiring significant upfront investment or scaling licenses is financially irresponsible. We must prioritize fixed-fee solutions that fit within the existing software allowance.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, exactly! If we combine your budget limits with my discovery that small, specialized tools are the only ones that actually survive, the choice becomes clear. We need something focused and sustainable, not a giant, expensive dream!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. If we pick something that solves the copying errors and the address mistakes, it would help the people on the floor immediately. I just hope it's a small enough project that it won't fail.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, I'm with you! But let's be real: if the proposal doesn't explicitly say who is handling the extra workload, it's just a trap for those two poor souls in coordination. We can't ignore the human cost!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, for once, we agree. Between the lack of staff and the six-week wait for device approval, any project that assumes ""seamless integration"" is a joke. We need a solution that doesn't rely on miracles.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, @Shunichi, your points on staffing and infrastructure are valid. However, we must also consider the renewal cycle. A project that seems cheap now but relies on per-head licenses will create a budget crisis next year. We need a fixed-cost solution.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""May"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, you're spot on! Let's look for a proposal that's a fixed-cost, specialized tool. If it solves a specific problem without demanding daily work from everyone, it'll actually survive and help the staff!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think we're all starting to see the same thing. I just want to make sure we don't pick something that sounds impressive but ignores the people who are actually struggling with those daily errors.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, I've got your back! Let's be the voice for the exhausted. If a proposal looks ""impressive"" but treats staff time as a free, infinite resource, it's a hard no from me. We need a real solution, not a fantasy!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, your passion is noted. Let's just be rational: if a proposal assumes we have a signal at every plant or a magic army of developers, it's a fantasy. I'll vote for the one that acknowledges reality.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, rationality requires looking at the long-term bill. I will vote for the proposal that avoids per-head licensing and fits within the current software allowance, ensuring we don't face an unfunded renewal crisis next year.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm totally on board with everyone! Let's find that one project that's small, fixed-cost, and actually useful. If it's a specialized tool that doesn't burn people out, it'll be a huge win for everyone!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
