60,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Um... looking at these, I think Proposal C, the Supplier Data Hub, is the best. It directly fixes the address mistakes and the copying of records I found. It seems small and focused, not like a fantasy.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, I'm totally with you on C! It solves those annoying errors without sounding like a massive, soul-crushing project. Plus, it doesn't seem to require a magic army of developers to keep it running.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, for once, your intuition is actually useful. Proposal A is a disaster waiting to happen given the dead zones and approval delays I found. C is the only one that doesn't rely on a miracle to function.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Daisuke, @May, @Shunichi, I agree. Proposal C is the most rational choice. It addresses specific inefficiencies and, unlike a mobile app or a broad assistant, it is likely a fixed-fee implementation that fits our current software allowance.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""May"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, @Shunichi, @May, @Daisuke, I'm in! Proposal C is a specialized tool for a specific problem, which is exactly what my research shows actually survives. It's the perfect fit for our budget and our people!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Shunichi"",""May"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,I... I'm glad we all agree. It feels right to choose something that actually helps the people dealing with those daily frustrations. I'll vote for Proposal C.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, you're welcome! I'm voting for C too. It's the only one that doesn't look like a trap for the staff. Let's give those exhausted people a break and actually fix something for them!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, let's not get carried away with the sentiment. I'm voting for C simply because it's the only option that doesn't assume our infrastructure is magically functional. It's the only rational choice.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, rationality is indeed the key. Proposal C avoids the scaling costs of per-head licenses and the risks of a frozen capital budget. It is the only sustainable option. I vote for Proposal C.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, @Shunichi, @May, @Daisuke, this is awesome! We've found a solution that's sustainable, realistic, and actually helpful. I'm voting for Proposal C too. Let's make this one a success!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Shunichi"",""May"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I... I feel much better now that we're all on the same page. Thank you for listening to my concerns. I'm definitely voting for Proposal C.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, of course! You were the one who pointed us in the right direction. I'm sticking with C. Let's just make sure the implementation doesn't secretly fall on those two poor souls in coordination!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, your obsession with those two clerks is almost impressive. Regardless, C is the only proposal that doesn't ignore the physical reality of our plants. I'm voting for C.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@May, we can monitor the implementation to prevent that. My priority remains the financial stability of the project. Proposal C is the only one that ensures we won't be blindsided by renewal costs. I maintain my vote for C.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Ryuji, @Shunichi, @May, @Daisuke, I'm so glad we're all in agreement! It's rare to be this unanimous. I'm voting for Proposal C because it's a specialized tool that actually has a chance to survive. Let's do this!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Ryuji"",""Shunichi"",""May"",""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm really happy we could find a solution that helps the staff. I'll cast my final vote for Proposal C. Thank you, everyone.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, you're the real MVP today! I'm casting my final vote for Proposal C. Let's hope this actually makes life easier for the people on the ground. Cheers to a win for the staff!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, let's save the cheers for when it actually works. I'm casting my final vote for Proposal C. It's the only one that doesn't treat our infrastructure like a fairy tale.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I have considered all the factors. Proposal C is the only choice that aligns with our financial constraints and avoids future budget crises. I cast my final vote for Proposal C.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,This has been a great team effort! I'm casting my final vote for Proposal C. It's a focused tool that fits our budget and our history of success. Let's make sure this one lasts!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
